<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  Vietnamese (vi) for :feature:settings. Mirrors values/strings.xml — MINUS the seventeen endonyms.

  WORDING BAN (LLM.md §1, §5) carries into every locale: no marketing claim and no performance
  percentage figures. Nothing on these six screens reports a measurement at all, so every string below
  either names a destination or explains what a permission is used for.

  WHY settings_language_* IS ABSENT FROM THIS FILE
  The seventeen endonyms are translatable="false" in values/strings.xml. An endonym is a language's
  name IN THAT LANGUAGE, and its only job is to be readable by someone who cannot read the current UI
  language — so "简体中文" must stay "简体中文" while the UI is Vietnamese, and "Tiếng Việt" must stay
  "Tiếng Việt" while the UI is Japanese. Overriding any of them here would defeat the picker. They
  resolve from values/ in every locale, which is exactly what translatable="false" asks for.

  settings_permission_* keeps the rationale rule: it states what the app does with the grant, and
  never that the user's device is at risk without it.
-->
